      "callouts": [
        {
          "sectionId": "pillar-8-8b-mcp-security-the-gap-almost-everyone-misses-k",
          "text": "Gap fill - MCP security:: The MCP spec explicitly does NOT enforce security. A malicious server can hide instructions in tool descriptions/responses that your model trusts as developer instructions (tool poisoning) - a supply-chain-style attack, worse than normal prompt injection. Defenses: treat servers like pinned dependencies (version + content hash), default read-only, re-approve after changes, sandbox execution, validate tool responses before they hit the context."
        }
      ],
